  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1010 PM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nA highly amplified pattern will develop mid-week developing an omega \nblock across the center of the CONUS. The blocking pattern will keep \nthe weather uneventful for the remainder of the week. This will \ncontinue to keep temperatures close to seasonal averages through the \nweek. A number of short wave troughs will drop southeastward around \nthe trough on the east side of the omega block this week. A few cold \nfronts may make it into the area with the first early on Wednesday \nand possibly a back door front on Friday. Conditions will change for \nthe upcoming weekend as the blocking pattern starts to break down \nand shift eastward. A short wave trough will rotate out of northern \nMexico this weekend around the larger trough covering the western \nCONUS. Guidance has trended to a negative tilt with this trough \nfavoring increasing precipitation chances.",
